<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stephen F. Austin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1793–1836</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stephen F. Austin (1793–1836) was an American empresario known as the Father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>. Taking over his father's grant from newly independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, he settled the first legal Anglo-American colonists in Texas from 1821 and managed a colony of thousands of families. Imprisoned in Mexico in 1834–1835, he joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas-revolution">Texas Revolution</a>, lost the presidential election of 1836 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sam-houston">Sam Houston</a> and died as the republic's secretary of state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stephen-f-austin.jpg" alt="Stephen F. Austin" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stephen_Fuller_Austin_Posthumous_Portrait.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
